        <h1 class="font-serif text-3xl lg:text-4xl text-ink leading-tight mb-5">What is Anxiety? Symptoms and How to Recognise It in Yourself</h1>
        <p class="text-ink-muted text-lg leading-relaxed">Constant tension, thoughts that won't let you sleep, a nameless dread you can't quite explain — these could all be signs of anxiety.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="py-12 bg-white">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-5 lg:px-8">
        <div class="prose-custom space-y-8">

          <div>
            <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl text-ink mb-4">What is anxiety?</h2>
            <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mb-4">The word "anxiety" comes from the Latin <em>anxietas</em> — meaning to be squeezed or choked. Medically, anxiety is an intense state of worry, fear or tension in response to a real or perceived threat.</p>
            <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mb-4">Some anxiety is completely normal. Nerves before an exam, excitement ahead of an important interview, apprehension when making a risky decision — these are all healthy, functional forms of anxiety. They motivate us and keep us safe.</p>
            <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">The problem arises when anxiety appears without a genuine threat, persists over time, or begins to disrupt everyday life.</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl text-ink mb-4">What are the symptoms of anxiety?</h2>
            <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mb-4">Anxiety symptoms fall into three groups: physical, emotional and behavioural.</p>
            <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
              <div class="bg-warm rounded-xl p-4 border border-warm-tertiary">
                <p class="text-xs font-medium text-ink mb-3">Physical</p>
                <ul class="text-xs text-ink-muted space-y-1.5">
                  <li>• Palpitations, racing heart</li>
                  <li>• Sweating, trembling</li>
                  <li>• Shortness of breath, choking feeling</li>
                  <li>• Nausea, digestive issues</li>
                  <li>• Muscle tension, headaches</li>
                  <li>• Sleep difficulties, chronic fatigue</li>
                </ul>
              </div>
              <div class="bg-warm rounded-xl p-4 border border-warm-tertiary">
                <p class="text-xs font-medium text-ink mb-3">Emotional</p>
                <ul class="text-xs text-ink-muted space-y-1.5">
                  <li>• Persistent sense of dread</li>
                  <li>• Feeling something will go wrong</li>
                  <li>• Irritability and tension</li>
                  <li>• Fear of losing control</li>
                  <li>• Difficulty concentrating</li>
                  <li>• Mind going blank</li>
                </ul>
              </div>
              <div class="bg-warm rounded-xl p-4 border border-warm-tertiary">
                <p class="text-xs font-medium text-ink mb-3">Behavioural</p>
                <ul class="text-xs text-ink-muted space-y-1.5">
                  <li>• Avoiding triggers</li>
                  <li>• Excessive checking or planning</li>
                  <li>• Seeking reassurance</li>
                  <li>• Withdrawing socially</li>
                  <li>• Procrastinating on anxious tasks</li>
                  <li>• Over-relying on distractions</li>
                </ul>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="bg-primary/5 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-primary/15">
            <p class="text-sm text-ink font-medium mb-2">How common is it?</p>
            <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">Approximately 1 in 4 people will experience an anxiety disorder at some point in their lives, making it the most common mental health condition globally. (WHO)</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl text-ink mb-4">Normal anxiety vs an anxiety disorder</h2>
            <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mb-4">The line can be hard to draw. The following factors suggest anxiety may have crossed into a clinical disorder:</p>
            <ul class="space-y-3">
              <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-primary shrink-0 mt-0.5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 12l2 2 4-4"></path></svg>
                <div>
                  <p class="text-sm font-medium text-ink">Duration: longer than six weeks</p>
                  <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted mt-0.5">If worry persists even after the stressor has passed, that is a significant signal.</p>
                </div>
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-primary shrink-0 mt-0.5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 12l2 2 4-4"></path></svg>
                <div>
                  <p class="text-sm font-medium text-ink">Disproportionate intensity</p>
                  <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted mt-0.5">When the level of worry is out of proportion to the actual threat and is hard to control.</p>
                </div>
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-primary shrink-0 mt-0.5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 12l2 2 4-4"></path></svg>
                <div>
                  <p class="text-sm font-medium text-ink">Disrupted daily functioning</p>
                  <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted mt-0.5">Work, relationships, sleep or social life are being negatively affected.</p>
                </div>
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-primary shrink-0 mt-0.5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 12l2 2 4-4"></path></svg>
                <div>
                  <p class="text-sm font-medium text-ink">Accompanying physical symptoms</p>
                  <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted mt-0.5">Persistent palpitations, sweating or shortness of breath that don't have another medical cause.</p>
                </div>
              </li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl text-ink mb-4">Do you have anxiety? Five questions to ask yourself</h2>
            <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mb-5">These questions are not a clinical diagnosis. They are a starting point to help you decide whether professional support might be useful.</p>
            <div class="space-y-3">
              <div class="flex gap-4 bg-warm rounded-xl p-4 border border-warm-tertiary">
                <span class="w-7 h-7 rounded-full bg-primary/10 text-primary text-xs font-semibold flex items-center justify-center shrink-0">1</span>
                <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted self-center">Have you felt anxious or on edge almost every day for the past six weeks?</p>
              </div>
              <div class="flex gap-4 bg-warm rounded-xl p-4 border border-warm-tertiary">
                <span class="w-7 h-7 rounded-full bg-primary/10 text-primary text-xs font-semibold flex items-center justify-center shrink-0">2</span>
                <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted self-center">Is it becoming difficult to stop or control the worry?</p>
              </div>
              <div class="flex gap-4 bg-warm rounded-xl p-4 border border-warm-tertiary">
                <span class="w-7 h-7 rounded-full bg-primary/10 text-primary text-xs font-semibold flex items-center justify-center shrink-0">3</span>
                <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted self-center">Has your sleep been disrupted, or do you feel constantly tired?</p>
              </div>
              <div class="flex gap-4 bg-warm rounded-xl p-4 border border-warm-tertiary">
                <span class="w-7 h-7 rounded-full bg-primary/10 text-primary text-xs font-semibold flex items-center justify-center shrink-0">4</span>
                <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted self-center">Is this affecting your work, relationships or social life?</p>
              </div>
              <div class="flex gap-4 bg-warm rounded-xl p-4 border border-warm-tertiary">
                <span class="w-7 h-7 rounded-full bg-primary/10 text-primary text-xs font-semibold flex items-center justify-center shrink-0">5</span>
                <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted self-center">Are you experiencing physical symptoms such as palpitations, sweating or shortness of breath?</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted mt-4 pl-1">If you answered yes to three or more, a psychological assessment could be a valuable next step.</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl text-ink mb-4">Can anxiety be treated?</h2>
            <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mb-4">Yes — with the right support, anxiety is highly manageable and often resolves fully. The main evidence-based approaches are:</p>
            <ul class="space-y-3">
              <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-primary shrink-0 mt-0.5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 12l2 2 4-4"></path></svg>
                <div>
                  <p class="text-sm font-medium text-ink">Cognitive Behavioural Therapy (CBT)</p>
                  <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted mt-0.5">Focuses on changing the thought patterns and avoidance behaviours that fuel anxiety. CBT has the strongest evidence base for anxiety treatment.</p>
                </div>
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-primary shrink-0 mt-0.5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 12l2 2 4-4"></path></svg>
                <div>
                  <p class="text-sm font-medium text-ink">EMDR</p>
                  <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted mt-0.5">Particularly effective for anxiety rooted in past traumatic experiences.</p>
                </div>
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-primary shrink-0 mt-0.5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 12l2 2 4-4"></path></svg>
                <div>
                  <p class="text-sm font-medium text-ink">Mindfulness-based approaches</p>
                  <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted mt-0.5">Anchoring attention to the present moment helps break the anxiety cycle and build body awareness.</p>
                </div>
              </li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div class="bg-accent/5 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-accent/15">
            <p class="text-sm text-ink font-medium mb-2">When should you seek help?</p>
            <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">If anxiety symptoms have lasted more than six weeks, are disrupting your daily functioning, or have led to avoidance behaviours, speaking with a psychologist is recommended. Early support makes treatment more straightforward.</p>
          </div>

        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
